_off} = 68\n- {final_children} = 12\n\nUsing the formula: 12 = 36 - 68 + {children_got_on}\n12 = -32 + {children_got_on}\n{children_got_on} = 12 + 32 = 44\n\nSo 68 children got off and 44 children got on.\nThe difference is 68 - 44 = 24.\n\nThe answer is 24"], "Programming Expert3bgF": ["```python\ndef bus_children_problem():\n    initial_children = 36\n    children_got_off = 68\n    final_children = 12\n    \n    # Using the formula: final = initial - got_off + got_on\n    # So: got_on = final - initial + got_off\n    children_got_on = final_children - initial_children + children_got_off\n    \n    # How many more got off than got on\n    difference = children_got_off - children_got_on\n    \n    return difference\n\nanswer = bus_children_problem()\n```\nthe answer is 24"], "Inspector4jEX": ["Looking at this problem, I need to find how many more children got off than got on.\n\n**Given information:**\n- Initial children on bus: 36\n- Children who got off: 68\n- Final children on bus: 12\n\n**My solving process:**\n\nLet x = number of children who got on the bus\n\nThe relationship is:\nInitial - Got off + Got on = Final\n36 - 68 + x = 12\n\nSolving for x:\n-32 + x = 12\nx = 12 + 32\nx = 44\n\nSo 44 children got on the bus.\n\nNow finding the difference (how many more got off than got on):\n68 - 44 = 24\n\n**Verification:**\n36 - 68 + 44 = 12\n-32 + 44 = 12 \u2713\n\n**Checking the agents' work:**\nBoth Agent 37oN and Agent 3bgF correctly:\n- Used the formula: got_on = final - initial + got_off = 12 - 36 + 68 = 44\n- Found the difference: 68 - 44 = 24\n- Verified their answer\n\nThe answer is 24"], "Math Solver8mNZ": ["We know the Answer Hints: 24 24 24 24 24 24. With the Answer Hints: 24, we will answer the question.  \nLet's think step by step.  \n\nInitially there are 36 children on the bus.  \nAt the bus stop, 68 children get off. Let the number of children who get on be \\(x\\).  \n\nAfter the stop, the number of children on the bus is  \n\\(36 - 68 + x = 12\\)